      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`BaseMultimodalProcessor.__init__` reads its options from the global server config, so a processor cannot be built outside a server.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add `MultimodalProcessorConfig` (image backend, `mm_process_config`, worker counts, media URL policy).\n- The base processor builds it from the server args and reads only the config afterwards.\n\n## Tests\n\nExisting processor tests.\n\n## Stack\n\nPart 2 of 9, based on part 1; review and merge in order.\n\n| Part | PR | Title |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1/9 | #43420 | Move multimodal enums to a shared module |\n| 2/9 | #46408 | Initialize multimodal processors from a processor config **(this PR)** |\n| 3/9 | #46409 | Extract a shared multimodal processor mixin |\n| 4/9 | #46410 | Split feature transport and preprocessing placement out of the base processor |\n| 5/9 | #46411 | Add a token-space multimodal processor |\n| 6/9 | #46412 | Serve token-space processors behind --enable-token-space-processor |\n| 7/9 | #46413 | Add a token-space strategy for Qwen VL models |\n| 8/9 | #46414 | Check token-space Qwen output against the legacy processor |\n| 9/9 | #46415 | Expand only the new turn of a multimodal request |\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40446230756](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40446230756)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40446230673](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40446230673)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40446230833](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40446230833)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
